Hi everyone,

I have installed RedHat 7.3 and wanted to set it up for packet.

I have recompiled the kernel to include AX25 / ROSE etc as well as kernel
support for the baycom and soundcard modems.  It all still boots up OK.

I have two problems.

First the kernel now doesn't seem to be able to find some of the libraries
it needs (eg for the ext3 filesystem) - I compiled the new kernel using the
following commands

make menuconfig
make dep
make clean
make bzImage
cp /usr/src/.../boot/bzImage /boot
make modules
make modules_install

do I have to specify a different initrd in grub as I do with the kernel?

I have attached a zip file containing dmesg, messages and .config (kernel)
for anyone who wants to assist me.

Secondly, I have had a look though the AX25 howto at
http://www.linux.org/docs/ldp/howto/AX25-HOWTO/index.html and had a look
though all my install disks for the AX25 files.  I have 3 install disks, 2
program source disks and a kernel source disk.  The AX25 files is on none of
them.

I got the ax25 ackages from sourceforge.  The libs tar.gz file uncompressed,
compiled and installed OK.  I uncompressed the tools package but could not
get it to compile.  A screendump s in the attached zip in a file called
errors.

Any help with these problems would be appreciated.

Michael
